## 5. Phase 1 — Frontend Reliability Fixes

Phase 1 addressed seven issues in the existing interface.

### 5.1 Bedside Kit

Corrected playlist presentation so the actual track name and label are displayed.

Removed misleading wording generated from raw backend fields, including phrases such as *because of reacted*.

### 5.2 Compare

Improved the handling of null, blank and empty fields.

The interface now avoids unnecessary empty placeholders while retaining meaningful comparison data.

### 5.3 Error Handling

Introduced endpoint-specific handling for missing resources.

A missing person, missing comparison and missing Wish Book now produce different messages.

### 5.4 Wish Book

Improved source separation and tag presentation.

Family-provided information is kept distinct from inferred information.

Visible tags are limited to five per item.

### 5.5 Things We Learned

Removed vague mood-only filler while retaining concrete observations.

### 5.6 Qloo Activity Log

Implemented more readable activity descriptions and preserved the ability to inspect raw log entries.

### 5.7 Wish Maker Cards

Improved maker labels, sample identification and explanations of Qloo, text and type-based matching.

